<title>FINLAND: ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results from the world ice</p>
<p>hockey championships on Saturday:</p>
<p>Bronze medal match</p>
<p>Czech Republic 4 Russia 3 (2-1 1-0 1-2)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Czech Republic - Rostislav Vlach (10:24), Vladimir Vujtek (</p>
<p>12:21), Martin Prochazka (26:45), Dopita (58:10)</p>
<p>Russia - Alexander Korolyuk (14:44), Yashin (40:58), Prokopiev</p>
<p>(48:49)</p>
<p>Penalties: Czech Republic 12 minutes, Russia 20</p>
<p>Attendance: 13,249</p>
<p>Relegation round (In Tampere):</p>
<p>Latvia 5 Slovakia 4 (2-2 2-1 1-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Latvia - Igor Bondarevs (6:25), Aigars Cipruss (16:09),</p>
<p>Olegs Znaroks (29:43), Aleksandrs Macijevskis (39:22),</p>
<p>Aleksandrs Kercs (52:30)</p>
<p>Slovakia - Lubomir Kolnik (5:07), Zdenko Ciger (13:01),</p>
<p>Daniel Babka (37:46), Jozef Stumpel (42:27)</p>
<p>Penalties: Latvia 6 minutes, Slovakia 10</p>
<p>Attendance: 7,287</p>
<p>Relegation round (Tampere):</p>
<p>Italy 8 France 1 (3-0 2-0 3-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Italy - Gaetano Orlando (4:04), Rob Nardella (8:22), Maurizio</p>
<p>Mansi (9:24, 22:17, 28:52), Christopher Bartolone (52:21, Roland</p>
<p>Ramoser (53:41), Markus Brunner (57:04)</p>
<p>France - Karl Dewolf (43:04)</p>
<p>Penalties: Italy 37 minutes, France 35</p>
<p>Attendance: 5,900</p>
<p>Relegation round final standings:</p>
<p>		    P  W  D  L  Pts</p>
<p> 1. Latvia	5  4  0  1   8</p>
<p> 2. Italy	 5  3  1  1   7</p>
<p> 3. Slovakia    5  3  0  2   6</p>
<p> 4. France	5  2  0  3   4</p>
<p> 5. Germany     5  2  0  3   4</p>
<p> 6. Norway	5  0  1  4   1</p>
<p>Norway relegated to pool B</p>
